    <!-- Privacy copy. Reviewed as a security control, not as marketing. -->
    <string name="notif_privacy_title">What is shared, and what is not</string>
    <string name="notif_privacy_body">Notifications from the apps you choose are sent in full to the computer you named, over the same direct, pinned connection as everything else — never to a cloud service. OmniBridge does not read, classify or hide anything inside a notification, and it keeps no history: nothing is written to this device or the computer. OmniBridge never shares its own notifications, and never shares a notification an app marks as private to the lock screen.</string>

